Stand down, Marine, or I will snap you like a twig!


00:58:26.036 --> 00:58:29.371
And she will keep company with any person she sees fit


00:58:29.373 --> 00:58:31.039
and you will treat her with respect,


00:58:31.041 --> 00:58:32.508
or you will not be permitted in her presence.


00:58:32.510 --> 00:58:33.542
Is that understood?


00:58:33.544 --> 00:58:35.110
Dayton, let him go!


00:58:35.112 --> 00:58:37.513
Let him go!
Dayton!


00:59:42.445 --> 00:59:44.112
All right, a dollar does it.


00:59:44.114 --> 00:59:46.048
Thank you very much, and you girls have a great day.


00:59:46.050 --> 00:59:47.115
Thanks, Ricky.


00:59:47.117 --> 00:59:48.750
Hello, Ma'am.
How can I help you?


00:59:48.752 --> 00:59:53.088
I was just thinkin' about havin' a cookie with nu...


00:59:53.090 --> 00:59:57.559
Well, hello, Ricky.
How are you?


01:00:02.298 --> 01:00:04.366
Ooh, strong.


01:00:04.368 --> 01:00:06.368
I like that.


01:00:06.370 --> 01:00:09.071
And that's why I like you, Ricky.


01:00:09.073 --> 01:00:11.173
You're strong.


01:00:11.175 --> 01:00:13.575
A-a strong person, I mean.


01:00:13.577 --> 01:00:15.010
Thank you.


01:00:15.012 --> 01:00:18.080
My daughter is not so strong.


01:00:18.082 --> 01:00:19.748
She never has been.


01:00:19.750 --> 01:00:22.484
She's more fragile.


01:00:22.486 --> 01:00:25.320
She never has had her heart broken.


01:00:25.322 --> 01:00:28.256
Her life's been pretty good.


01:00:28.258 --> 01:00:30.926
And you think mine hasn't?


01:00:30.928 --> 01:00:34.429
Well, now, I didn't say that.


01:00:34.431 --> 01:00:37.766
I know you have a lotta people who love you very much.


01:00:37.768 --> 01:00:40.502
That is plain to see.


01:00:40.504 --> 01:00:42.304
But I suspect,


01:00:42.306 --> 01:00:46.742
and forgive me if I am wrong, but I suspect


01:00:46.744 --> 01:00:50.612
that you've had your fair share of hard knocks


01:00:50.614 --> 01:00:53.248
that you've had to rise above


01:00:53.250 --> 01:00:57.452
to become the luminous young...


01:00:58.621 --> 01:01:02.658
lady that you clearly are.


01:01:04.093 --> 01:01:07.329
You don't want Francesca.


01:01:07.331 --> 01:01:10.365
You have your eye on someone else.


01:01:10.367 --> 01:01:14.569
That is also plain to see to anyone.


01:01:14.571 --> 01:01:18.907
Let her down, sooner than later, please?


01:01:18.909 --> 01:01:24.446
I have no doubt that your affection for her is genuine,


01:01:24.448 --> 01:01:29.551
but we both know this is not a forever thing


01:01:29.553 --> 01:01:34.322
and she has a wedding to prepare for.


01:01:35.324 --> 01:01:38.427
One final word of advice.


01:01:39.595 --> 01:01:42.130
Beautiful women


01:01:42.132 --> 01:01:47.602
are the only women who get heard in this world.


01:01:47.604 --> 01:01:50.572
You have that goin' for you,


01:01:51.541 --> 01:01:53.241
but should it ever come up,


01:01:54.343 --> 01:02:00.082
transgender just sounds so...
ugly.


01:02:01.951 --> 01:02:04.720
You'd be better off just tellin' everybody


01:02:04.722 --> 01:02:07.522
you have a birth defect.


01:02:10.493 --> 01:02:12.327
Thank you, Helen.


01:02:12.329 --> 01:02:14.930
Sage words, indeed.


01:02:17.166 --> 01:02:22.070
Is that what you tell people is your excuse?


01:03:27.303 --> 01:03:28.703
Did you sleep with her?


01:03:28.705 --> 01:03:30.305
It's none of your business.


01:03:30.307 --> 01:03:31.339
Don't you walk away from me, freak.


01:03:31.341 --> 01:03:33.308
Keep your hands off me.
Fuck off, David.


01:03:33.310 --> 01:03:35.343
A lady doesn't kiss and tell.
Why should I?


01:03:35.345 --> 01:03:37.379
You are not a lady!


01:03:41.818 --> 01:03:43.118
I swear to God,


01:03:43.120 --> 01:03:48.089
if you had sex with my fiancée, I will fuckin' kill you.


01:03:48.091 --> 01:03:50.625
You like bein' on top of me, David?


01:03:50.627 --> 01:03:51.827
From what I can recall,


01:03:51.829 --> 01:03:54.262
you like bein' on the bottom much more.


01:04:05.341 --> 01:04:07.175
Did you tell her?


01:04:07.177 --> 01:04:08.610
Course not.


01:04:08.612 --> 01:04:12.547
I mean, she doesn't even think I know who you are.


01:04:12.549 --> 01:04:14.416
Your secret's safe with me.


01:04:14.418 --> 01:04:16.885
I'm great with secrets.


01:04:16.887 --> 01:04:19.988
Look, you took my virginity,


01:04:19.990 --> 01:04:25.193
and to this day, are the only man I have ever slept with.


01:04:25.195 --> 01:04:29.097
So no matter how much of an asshole you can be,


01:04:31.000 --> 01:04:33.969
you'll always be special to me.


01:04:45.948 --> 01:04:47.582
David!


01:04:47.584 --> 01:04:49.050
David!


01:04:50.786 --> 01:04:52.153
Wha--


01:04:53.689 --> 01:04:55.323
Did he hurt you?


01:04:55.325 --> 01:04:56.324
No!


01:04:56.326 --> 01:04:57.626
No, he didn't. No.


01:04:57.628 --> 01:04:59.628
What is going on?


01:05:00.563 --> 01:05:01.763
You should talk to David.


01:05:01.765 --> 01:05:03.198
I'm asking you what is going on!


01:05:03.200 --> 01:05:05.567
You should talk to David.


01:05:09.572 --> 01:05:13.141
You haven't been returnin' my texts or my calls.


01:05:15.378 --> 01:05:17.512
I've just had a lot on my mind the past few days.


01:05:17.514 --> 01:05:19.314
I-I'm sorry.


01:05:25.388 --> 01:05:27.389
You don't wanna see me anymore, do you?


01:05:29.425 --> 01:05:31.159
I like you so much.


01:05:31.161 --> 01:05:32.794
I know you do.


01:05:32.796 --> 01:05:34.496
But...


01:05:36.766 --> 01:05:38.466
You do not need to explain.


01:05:38.468 --> 01:05:39.534
And you wouldn't want me anyway.


01:05:39.536 --> 01:05:40.535
Please don't tell me what I want.


01:05:40.537 --> 01:05:42.771
I can't give you babies.
I-I can't--


01:05:42.773 --> 01:05:45.073
Please don't tell me what I want.


01:05:50.279 --> 01:05:52.714
I wasn't thinkin' about the future.


01:05:55.117 --> 01:05:59.454
For once in my life, I was just thinkin' about right now.


01:06:01.791 --> 01:06:03.124
Here.


01:06:07.430 --> 01:06:09.064
It's amazing.


01:06:10.733 --> 01:06:13.335
Here.
So electric.


01:06:16.739 --> 01:06:19.808
It's a wonder more people don't visit, here.


01:06:26.615 --> 01:06:29.517
But it hurts more, too.


01:06:30.453 --> 01:06:32.053
Here.


01:06:37.693 --> 01:06:40.795
I guess it's just easier to just stay way over there


01:06:40.797 --> 01:06:44.099
with the Marine, stay-at-home mom.


01:06:52.074 --> 01:06:56.177
You are gonna do great things in New York.


01:06:56.179 --> 01:06:58.513
I haven't even opened it yet.
I'm too scared.


01:06:58.515 --> 01:07:01.082
Oh, don't be scared.
You'll get in.


01:07:01.084 --> 01:07:02.517
Thanks.


01:07:06.022 --> 01:07:08.123
We can still be friends, can't we?


01:07:11.093 --> 01:07:12.527
Maybe someday.


01:07:14.163 --> 01:07:15.764
Francesca...


01:07:15.766 --> 01:07:18.033
Don't feel bad.


01:07:18.035 --> 01:07:19.601
You did nothin' wrong.


01:07:21.704 --> 01:07:24.706
I'm so much better for havin' known you.


01:08:32.041 --> 01:08:33.241
Who is it?


01:08:33.243 --> 01:08:35.076
It's me.


01:08:35.078 --> 01:08:37.011
What are you doin' here?


01:08:37.013 --> 01:08:39.013
What do ya mean?
It's TV night.


01:08:41.550 --> 01:08:43.318
Can I come in?


01:08:43.320 --> 01:08:46.087
Um, yeah.


01:08:46.589 --> 01:08:48.756
Yeah, sure, come in.


01:08:56.632 --> 01:08:58.166
- Hey.
- Hey.


01:08:58.168 --> 01:08:59.134
How ya doin'?


01:08:59.136 --> 01:09:01.436
I'm great.
How are you?


01:09:02.571 --> 01:09:04.305
I'm fine.


01:09:08.043 --> 01:09:13.348
Heard you, uh, broke it off with Francesca.


01:09:13.350 --> 01:09:15.016
How'd ya hear that?


01:09:15.584 --> 01:09:17.285
Well, it's a small town.


01:09:18.154 --> 01:09:20.155
You're you.


01:09:21.423 --> 01:09:25.126
Yeah, well, guess that's true, huh?


01:09:32.535 --> 01:09:34.736
You don't seem very upset.


01:09:34.738 --> 01:09:36.237
Course I am.


01:09:36.239 --> 01:09:38.206
I mean it sucks, but shit happens.


01:09:38.208 --> 01:09:39.774
Two people can like each other,


01:09:39.776 --> 01:09:42.777
but it's not always gonna be enough.


01:09:42.779 --> 01:09:46.281
So you gotta break up.


01:09:46.283 --> 01:09:47.649
Really quickly.


01:09:47.651 --> 01:09:49.117
Right?


01:09:49.119 --> 01:09:50.351
And that's that?


01:09:50.353 --> 01:09:52.754
Yup. Pretty much.


01:09:52.756 --> 01:09:55.857
What else am I supposed to do?
Mope around for a month?


01:09:55.859 --> 01:09:59.661
And, you know, I'll be damned if I'm gonna let hormones


01:09:59.663 --> 01:10:01.062
get me all emotional about this, you know?


01:10:01.064 --> 01:10:02.797
You know, you can be as much of a bitch


01:10:02.799 --> 01:10:05.433
as any biological girl I've ever met.


01:10:06.402 --> 01:10:08.136
And by the way, it's not true


01:10:08.138 --> 01:10:11.005
that men are the ones who cut and run.


01:10:11.007 --> 01:10:14.943
Girls are the ones who flip that
switch and are onto the next.


01:10:14.945 --> 01:10:16.477
The real truth is we get our hearts broken


01:10:16.479 --> 01:10:18.746
and we stay crushed but...


01:10:20.049 --> 01:10:22.450
not you.


01:10:22.452 --> 01:10:25.453
That part of you is apparently all girl.


01:10:25.455 --> 01:10:28.890
You know, Robbie, I'm sure I would get my heart broken


01:10:28.892 --> 01:10:31.793
if I really did care for someone, and they left me.


01:10:31.795 --> 01:10:35.363
So you didn't really care for Francesca?


01:10:35.365 --> 01:10:37.365
What-what-what-what was that, then?


01:10:37.367 --> 01:10:40.268
Just some, what, fun toy experiment?


01:10:40.270 --> 01:10:44.339
No! No, she wasn't!
I was very fond of her!


01:10:44.341 --> 01:10:46.207
In spite of the fact that I've never been into girls,


01:10:46.209 --> 01:10:47.442
I honestly tried


01:10:47.444 --> 01:10:49.911
because I was so fucking fond of her.


01:10:49.913 --> 01:10:52.447
And no, you know what?
I didn't love her.


01:10:52.449 --> 01:10:54.582
When I figured that out, I cut her loose to be kind,


01:10:54.584 --> 01:10:56.117
and why the fuck are you giving me


01:10:56.119 --> 01:10:57.252
such a hard time about this anyway?


01:10:57.254 --> 01:10:58.553
Because, you know, you skate through life


01:10:58.555 --> 01:11:00.622
all la-di-da, not a care in the world,


01:11:00.624 --> 01:11:02.056
when you leave bodies in your wake.


01:11:02.058 --> 01:11:03.524
You know, it's like you think you're exempt


01:11:03.526 --> 01:11:05.059
because you're not a rea--


01:11:09.865 --> 01:11:12.200
'Cuz I'm not a real what?


01:11:13.669 --> 01:11:15.670
Whatever.


01:11:15.672 --> 01:11:17.305
No.


01:11:17.307 --> 01:11:19.173
No, not whatever.


01:11:19.708 --> 01:11:21.376
Say it.


01:11:21.378 --> 01:11:24.579
"I think I'm exempt because I'm not a real what?"


01:11:24.581 --> 01:11:25.947
- I'll talk to you later.
- No!


01:11:25.949 --> 01:11:27.382
Finish it!


01:11:27.384 --> 01:11:30.451
"I think I'm exempt because I'm not a real what?"


01:11:30.453 --> 01:11:32.553
You're not a real anything, okay?


01:11:32.555 --> 01:11:33.655
You're not a real anything!


01:11:33.657 --> 01:11:36.024
You're not a boy and you're not a girl.


01:11:46.802 --> 01:11:49.504
You're right.


01:11:49.506 --> 01:11:51.472
I'm not a real anything.


01:11:53.909 --> 01:11:55.777
So wha-Ricky, neither are any of us.


01:11:55.779 --> 01:11:59.080
That-that-that-that doesn't
give you the right to be unkind!


01:11:59.082 --> 01:12:02.083
You know, you-you-you think you have the market cornered


01:12:02.085 --> 01:12:03.985
on feeling alienated?


01:12:03.987 --> 01:12:06.321
I mean, shit, no matter what we look like or who we are,


01:12:06.323 --> 01:12:08.623
we're all just stumblin' through life


01:12:08.625 --> 01:12:11.426
trying to figure this shit out, just like you!


01:12:14.363 --> 01:12:18.199
Yeah, but, you know, unlike me,


01:12:18.201 --> 01:12:21.235
you all have an "us," to figure it out with.


01:12:21.237 --> 01:12:25.106
My "us"?
It's just me, Robbie.


01:12:26.041 --> 01:12:27.475
Try that some time.


01:12:27.477 --> 01:12:28.509
Lemme know how it works for you.


01:12:28.511 --> 01:12:30.078
No, no, no!
See, there you go again!


01:12:30.080 --> 01:12:31.279
It's all about you, isn't it?


01:12:31.281 --> 01:12:33.514
It's always all about you!


01:12:33.516 --> 01:12:36.651
Have you forgotten that I have been on your side,


01:12:36.653 --> 01:12:39.487
only on your side, without condition,


01:12:39.489 --> 01:12:41.789
since we were six years old!


01:12:42.758 --> 01:12:46.994
Of course I've never forgotten that, Robbie.


01:12:46.996 --> 01:12:49.397
And that's why I've always trusted


01:12:49.399 --> 01:12:51.733
that you were the only person in this world


01:12:51.735 --> 01:12:55.403
who didn't secretly feel this way about me.


01:12:55.405 --> 01:12:59.907
So now I guess my, "me," just got even smaller, huh?


01:12:59.909 --> 01:13:01.776
No big deal, though.


01:13:02.678 --> 01:13:05.313
I'm used to it.


01:13:06.349 --> 01:13:10.418
No, really, everything is just fine.


01:13:19.361 --> 01:13:21.796
Oh, what the fuck...
Excuse me, Buddy.


01:13:21.798 --> 01:13:23.264
- Will you look at somethin'?
- No, I got to go.


01:13:23.266 --> 01:13:26.100
Please! Please.


01:13:26.102 --> 01:13:27.368
All right.


01:13:29.305 --> 01:13:32.807
You shouldn't be goin' through people's private things.


01:13:32.809 --> 01:13:35.343
I help her when she makes her fashion videos.


01:13:35.345 --> 01:13:39.447
I accidentally found this, but I was afraid to show Dad.


01:13:42.117 --> 01:13:44.152
Okay.


01:14:14.383 --> 01:14:16.317
I thought your mom died of cancer.


01:14:16.319 --> 01:14:18.052
So did I.


01:14:37.172 --> 01:14:39.540
Wait, it's not over!


01:15:41.436 --> 01:15:43.271
Ricky, it's me.
Please call me back, okay?


01:15:43.273 --> 01:15:45.106
Please.


01:15:45.108 --> 01:15:46.340
I'm sorry!


01:15:59.154 --> 01:16:01.322
Mike, Mike, have you seen Ricky?


01:16:01.324 --> 01:16:03.124
Not tonight.


01:16:09.097 --> 01:16:10.731
Ricky!


01:16:11.867 --> 01:16:13.734
Ricky!


01:16:18.206 --> 01:16:19.740
Ricky!


01:16:21.143 --> 01:16:22.376
Ricky!


01:16:30.452 --> 01:16:31.485
Ricky!


01:16:32.120 --> 01:16:33.354
Ricky!


01:16:35.457 --> 01:16:36.490
Ricky!


01:16:40.796 --> 01:16:42.196
Ricky!


01:16:42.198 --> 01:16:44.131
What's all this shoutin' about?


01:16:44.133 --> 01:16:45.700
Oh, my God!


01:16:45.702 --> 01:16:47.735
Oh my G--
Are you okay?


01:16:47.737 --> 01:16:49.370
Yeah, I told you I'm fine.


01:16:52.574 --> 01:16:55.276
I saw the, uh--


01:16:55.978 --> 01:16:58.312
You saw what?


01:16:58.314 --> 01:17:02.350
I saw that video you-you made when you were younger.


01:17:02.352 --> 01:17:03.384
About your mother.


01:17:03.386 --> 01:17:05.052
You hacked into my computer?


01:17:05.054 --> 01:17:08.089
No, Sam found it by accident.


01:17:08.091 --> 01:17:10.791
Don't-don't be mad at him.


01:17:10.793 --> 01:17:12.793
He was scared.


01:17:12.795 --> 01:17:13.861
I was scared.


01:17:13.863 --> 01:17:15.563
Why?


01:17:16.698 --> 01:17:19.667
It seemed like-like you could hurt yourself.


01:17:19.669 --> 01:17:22.570
Well, now you know all my secrets.


01:17:23.839 --> 01:17:26.374
Ricky, why didn't you tell me any of those things?


01:17:26.376 --> 01:17:28.242
Because you're my only friend,


01:17:28.244 --> 01:17:31.545
and if you thought I was crazy
or something, I'd be all alone.


01:17:31.547 --> 01:17:33.114
I couldn't risk it.


01:17:33.116 --> 01:17:35.549
Oh, I still woulda been your friend.


01:17:38.120 --> 01:17:41.022
You be very careful right now, Robbie.


01:17:41.990 --> 01:17:43.557
And I'm so sorry for those things


01:17:43.559 --> 01:17:45.092
that I-I said to you, Ricky.


01:17:45.094 --> 01:17:46.160
I didn't mean any of 'em.


01:17:46.162 --> 01:17:50.798
You are not confused at all.


01:17:50.800 --> 01:17:56.270
You are the most unconfused person I know.


01:17:56.272 --> 01:17:58.339
And I didn't realize it at the time,


01:17:58.341 --> 01:18:05.179
but I was completely jealous of Francesca.


01:18:07.115 --> 01:18:12.620
I mean, you've had crushes before, but


01:18:14.489 --> 01:18:16.490
nothin' like that.


01:18:17.759 --> 01:18:23.064
To see you look at someone else like that,


01:18:25.901 --> 01:18:30.304
it just--
it just made me crazy.


01:18:34.876 --> 01:18:40.681
You are so beautiful, Ricky.


01:19:08.944 --> 01:19:12.346
You still think I'm beautiful?


01:19:27.028 --> 01:19:29.063
Are you scared?


01:19:29.865 --> 01:19:31.365
It's okay if you're a little scared.


01:19:31.367 --> 01:19:32.700
I'm a little scared.


01:19:32.702 --> 01:19:35.035
I'm not.


01:19:35.037 --> 01:19:38.005
I love you, Ricky.


01:19:38.740 --> 01:19:40.975
It's okay if you wanna ignore...


01:19:41.910 --> 01:19:46.614
I don't want to ignore anything about you,


01:19:47.616 --> 01:19:49.617
ever again.


01:19:59.961 --> 01:20:02.229
Do you love me?


01:20:02.231 --> 01:20:04.298
I've always loved you, Robbie.


01:20:04.300 --> 01:20:06.967
Since the day you ran away from that pervert I thought,


01:20:06.969 --> 01:20:08.536
"Now, that's a keeper."


01:20:16.178 --> 01:20:18.078
What do you want me to do?


01:20:19.414 --> 01:20:22.716
Well, let's start with...


01:20:29.658 --> 01:20:31.225
How's that sound?


01:20:32.260 --> 01:20:33.994
Yeah, pretty-pretty good.


01:20:35.998 --> 01:20:39.700
But, uh, I swear to you, Robby Riley,


01:20:39.702 --> 01:20:41.669
if you smell like fish, I will vomit on you.


01:20:41.671 --> 01:20:43.037
Okay, mood killer.


01:20:44.841 --> 01:20:46.640
Oh, I think you'll recover just fine.


01:20:46.642 --> 01:20:48.742
You know, I don't know, I mean,


01:20:48.744 --> 01:20:51.178
I'm already just a little bit outta my comfort zone here,


01:20:51.180 --> 01:20:53.547
and if you're gonna start crackin'...


01:20:55.650 --> 01:20:56.851
All right.


01:21:29.651 --> 01:21:31.552
So did that, uh...


01:21:34.789 --> 01:21:37.091
did that feel good to you?


01:21:37.093 --> 01:21:38.726
Last night?


01:21:39.794 --> 01:21:40.794
Yeah.


01:21:40.796 --> 01:21:46.734
You, uh, you're amazingly good with your hands.


01:21:48.069 --> 01:21:49.803
Well, I've had a lotta practice.


01:22:00.715 --> 01:22:03.150
Are you freaked out?


01:22:07.390 --> 01:22:13.394
Maybe a little, but it's just
because it's so new, you know?


01:22:13.396 --> 01:22:16.997
I-I just...
just never thought about...


01:22:20.035 --> 01:22:22.569
you know, before.


01:22:25.106 --> 01:22:26.640
Do you regret it?


01:22:32.013 --> 01:22:34.581
How could I regret realizing I'm in love


01:22:34.583 --> 01:22:36.784
with the hottest girl in town?


01:22:38.553 --> 01:22:41.722
Who just so happens to be my best friend.


01:22:43.091 --> 01:22:44.692
Hmm?


01:22:56.504 --> 01:22:59.239
I didn't get into the Fashion Institute.


01:22:59.241 --> 01:23:00.441
I know.


01:23:01.242 --> 01:23:04.178
I saw that stupid letter.


01:23:04.180 --> 01:23:07.047
I'm so sorry.
You'll go to New York anyway.


01:23:08.283 --> 01:23:12.086
Puttin' out a clothing line takes a lotta money.


01:23:12.088 --> 01:23:13.988
I don't even have enough to go to New York,


01:23:13.990 --> 01:23:16.123
let alone put out a clothing line.


01:23:16.125 --> 01:23:18.292
So, you'll get a job.


01:23:18.294 --> 01:23:23.030
Like millions of other aspiring artists do every year.


01:23:23.032 --> 01:23:24.665
And you'll make your clothes on the weekends,


01:23:24.667 --> 01:23:26.300
just like you do now.
I mean it--


01:23:26.302 --> 01:23:28.802
I just don't have it in me, Robbie.


01:23:28.804 --> 01:23:32.039
I know it seems like it doesn't, but it...


01:23:32.041 --> 01:23:34.908
it takes so much for me to put a smile on my face


01:23:34.910 --> 01:23:38.245
and go out in the world every day.


01:23:38.247 --> 01:23:41.715
And that's here, you know, where people know me.


01:23:41.717 --> 01:23:44.051
And like me.


01:23:44.053 --> 01:23:46.053
I'll just stay here.


01:23:47.222 --> 01:23:49.957
And I got you now.


01:23:49.959 --> 01:23:51.925
Life wouldn't be so bad.


01:23:54.629 --> 01:23:58.098
It was just a silly dream anyway.


01:23:58.100 --> 01:24:00.567
Most people give up on their dreams, you know?


01:24:00.569 --> 01:24:03.203
It's not the end of the world.


01:24:55.657 --> 01:24:59.126
I'm so sorry I cheated on you.


01:25:01.563 --> 01:25:03.097
That was wrong.


01:25:04.899 --> 01:25:06.500
Of course, that was wrong.


01:25:06.502 --> 01:25:08.135
Can you forgive me?


01:25:14.209 --> 01:25:16.243
Are you in love with her?


01:25:21.716 --> 01:25:23.984
I love so many things about her.


01:25:26.554 --> 01:25:28.956
But am I in love with her, and...


01:25:30.492 --> 01:25:34.495
...do I see myself with her forever?


01:25:34.497 --> 01:25:36.630
No, probably not.


01:25:43.304 --> 01:25:46.039
Are you still in love with me?


01:25:49.277 --> 01:25:51.111
I am.


01:25:52.013 --> 01:25:55.349
Can you still see a life forever with me?


01:26:02.490 --> 01:26:04.324
I don't know.


01:26:08.763 --> 01:26:11.331
I don't like how you can hate.


01:26:13.201 --> 01:26:15.469
I mean, I understand it has to be part of your job,


01:26:15.471 --> 01:26:18.872
and your job protects us, and it keeps us safe,


01:26:18.874 --> 01:26:20.607
and for that, I'm forever grateful,


01:26:20.609 --> 01:26:22.809
and-and I think you're heroic,


01:26:22.811 --> 01:26:28.182
but people like Ricky are not the enemy.


01:26:30.752 --> 01:26:33.954
There's no reason to hate here.


01:26:33.956 --> 01:26:37.057
And I don't know if you can ever
change that part of yourself.


01:26:41.129 --> 01:26:42.863
I slept with her.


01:26:45.800 --> 01:26:47.501
Wha-you slept with who?


01:26:49.470 --> 01:26:51.705
Ricky.


01:26:54.742 --> 01:26:57.010
My sophomore year.


01:26:58.413 --> 01:27:01.648
Right before you and I started datin', actually.


01:27:02.684 --> 01:27:04.518
What do you mean you slept with her?


01:27:04.520 --> 01:27:07.321
We did everything there is to do.


01:27:11.726 --> 01:27:15.329
So, no, I don't hate her.


01:27:16.631 --> 01:27:18.665
And if you don't hate me for doin' it,


01:27:18.667 --> 01:27:20.467
it might go a long way towards me


01:27:20.469 --> 01:27:22.502
not hatin' myself for doin' it either.


01:27:22.504 --> 01:27:25.272
Of course I don't hate you.


01:27:32.747 --> 01:27:34.648
Hmm.


01:27:34.650 --> 01:27:37.484
How come you never told me?


01:27:40.188 --> 01:27:41.989
Right.


01:27:43.191 --> 01:27:45.025
And even Robbie never knew?


01:27:45.027 --> 01:27:46.693
No one did.


01:27:48.663 --> 01:27:50.897
We were very careful.


01:27:55.236 --> 01:27:56.770
Did you like it?


01:27:58.940 --> 01:28:02.409
Do you wanna do it again?


01:28:02.411 --> 01:28:05.479
I liked some things about it.


01:28:06.614 --> 01:28:09.016
But really, I just liked her.


01:28:09.884 --> 01:28:11.184
A lot.


01:28:12.220 --> 01:28:15.622
And I wanted to be as close with her as possible,


01:28:15.624 --> 01:28:22.029
so one night I... we...


01:28:22.031 --> 01:28:23.897
Mm-hmm.


01:28:24.799 --> 01:28:29.703
But, no, I-I've thought about it a lot,


01:28:29.705 --> 01:28:32.873
and I don't need to do it again.


01:28:45.787 --> 01:28:48.088
How 'bout this...


01:28:50.058 --> 01:28:55.662
how 'bout we'll postpone the wedding,


01:28:55.664 --> 01:29:02.469
not call it off, just, just
postpone it for a little while.


01:29:02.471 --> 01:29:04.805
And get to know each other again?


01:29:05.740 --> 01:29:08.442
Starting now.


01:29:08.444 --> 01:29:10.844
The real us, not...


01:29:10.846 --> 01:29:13.647
not the, "us," everybody told us we were.


01:29:15.917 --> 01:29:21.021
And then, ask me again and, um,


01:29:21.023 --> 01:29:24.591
I'm pretty sure I'll say yes.


01:29:44.313 --> 01:29:46.213
Hold your horses, I'm comin'.


01:29:46.215 --> 01:29:48.081
Well, come on, now, you're gonna be late for work.


01:29:48.083 --> 01:29:51.151
'Cause your dad's waitin' on me
at a parts' store in Otter Creek


01:29:51.153 --> 01:29:53.387
and he will not be happy.


01:29:53.389 --> 01:29:55.222
Let's go!


01:29:56.357 --> 01:29:59.159
Let Ricky know she's got some mail.


01:29:59.161 --> 01:30:01.261
All right, you got it, Joe.
Thank you.


01:30:04.600 --> 01:30:06.533
Come on!


01:30:11.172 --> 01:30:12.739
Okay.


01:30:12.741 --> 01:30:14.074
Let's go.


01:30:15.777 --> 01:30:18.478
What? I thought we were in such a hurry.
Let's go.


01:30:18.480 --> 01:30:20.347
I don't even get a kiss hello anymore?


01:30:20.349 --> 01:30:21.915
That's it, a-after a week together,


01:30:21.917 --> 01:30:23.116
we're just some old married couple,


01:30:23.118 --> 01:30:24.384
all the magic's gone?


01:30:24.386 --> 01:30:25.786
Well, you know, if you'd gotten here on time,


01:30:25.788 --> 01:30:28.321
than just a little ole married couple kiss.


01:30:28.323 --> 01:30:29.156
Oh, really?


01:30:29.158 --> 01:30:33.193
A little ole married couple quickie BJ.


01:30:33.195 --> 01:30:35.662
But you missed your chance.


01:30:36.664 --> 01:30:39.866
Okay, but seriously, I can't be late, let's go.


01:30:39.868 --> 01:30:41.234
Don't you think you should check your mail?


01:30:41.236 --> 01:30:42.702
For what? No.


01:30:42.704 --> 01:30:45.405
Oh, I-I mean, you should check your mail.


01:30:45.407 --> 01:30:46.807
That was kinda mean, actually.


01:30:46.809 --> 01:30:49.075
Well, now, wait a minute, I'm not being mean.


01:30:49.077 --> 01:30:50.210
I just, you know,


01:30:50.212 --> 01:30:51.778
I think you should just check your mail, that's all.


01:30:51.780 --> 01:30:53.229
Why?
What's goin' on?


01:30:54.382 --> 01:31:00.020
Nothin', Ricky, I ju-Look,
Joe just came by, he put some...


01:31:00.022 --> 01:31:01.421
just check.


01:31:02.490 --> 01:31:03.557
Please?


01:31:24.846 --> 01:31:28.014
- What the--
- What is it?


01:31:56.477 --> 01:31:58.612
Okay, what the hell's goin' on?


01:31:58.614 --> 01:32:00.647
- Oh, somethin' interesting?
- What did you do?


01:32:00.649 --> 01:32:02.516
Why are people sending me money?


01:32:02.518 --> 01:32:03.517
Ricky, Ricky.


01:32:03.519 --> 01:32:05.085
Ricky, look.


01:32:05.087 --> 01:32:06.286
Okay, that's it for today's video.


01:32:06.288 --> 01:32:07.354
Before I go, I wanted to talk to you


01:32:07.356 --> 01:32:08.288
about the outfit that I'm wearin'


01:32:08.290 --> 01:32:10.190
because I'm wearing a dress.
What?


01:32:10.192 --> 01:32:12.692
Why?
I know, because I like it.


01:32:12.694 --> 01:32:14.261
It was made by this girl named Ricky,


01:32:14.263 --> 01:32:16.196
who's a fashion designer from Kentucky.


01:32:16.198 --> 01:32:17.364
She didn't get accepted into


01:32:17.366 --> 01:32:19.900
some fancy New York fashion school,


01:32:19.902 --> 01:32:22.068
and now she is discouraged about the fashion line


01:32:22.070 --> 01:32:24.604
that she wants to make eventually in her life.


01:32:24.606 --> 01:32:28.341
So I am going to send one dollar bill to Ricky


01:32:28.343 --> 01:32:31.545
in helping with her to create her fashion line


01:32:31.547 --> 01:32:33.580
and I encourage you to do the same


01:32:33.582 --> 01:32:36.116
if you feel strongly about this.


01:32:36.118 --> 01:32:38.752
I think that she could be a really great designer


01:32:38.754 --> 01:32:42.422
and I wanna support that, so Ricky, here's to you.


01:32:42.424 --> 01:32:44.824
And that's the end of this video.
Bye!


01:32:44.826 --> 01:32:47.093
Couldn't fit it all in the truck.


01:32:47.095 --> 01:32:50.196
David and Francesca were kind enough to help.


01:32:54.702 --> 01:32:58.071
I hope you don't mind.
Well, it was Robbie's idea,


01:32:58.073 --> 01:33:01.174
but I thought if we maybe sent her the dress.


01:33:01.176 --> 01:33:03.543
Not that I didn't love it, of course.


01:33:06.581 --> 01:33:09.683
We wish you the very best of luck in New York, Ricky.


01:33:11.285 --> 01:33:12.552
We really do.


01:33:13.888 --> 01:33:15.722
Well, thank you.


01:33:18.159 --> 01:33:21.094
All right, there's the last of it, I think.


01:33:23.431 --> 01:33:26.266
Oh, I'm so proud of you.


01:33:29.370 --> 01:33:33.573
I know that you've always thought that she didn't, um,


01:33:33.575 --> 01:33:36.343
you know, totally approve,


01:33:36.345 --> 01:33:40.213
but that's something that you'd do well to let go of.


01:33:40.215 --> 01:33:43.817
You used to cry somethin' fierce in the night,


01:33:43.819 --> 01:33:45.385
and the only thing that would soothe you


01:33:45.387 --> 01:33:47.988
was her whispering in your ear over and over,


01:33:50.157 --> 01:33:55.295
"You are perfect in every way, sweet boy."


01:33:56.831 --> 01:34:00.367
She woulda said sweet girl if she could of.


01:34:00.369 --> 01:34:05.238
- I know that in my head, but--
- Well, know it in your heart.


01:34:05.240 --> 01:34:07.340
Because life is short.


01:34:09.810 --> 01:34:11.778
There ain't no time to waste it on things


01:34:11.780 --> 01:34:13.680
that are not the truth.


01:34:15.149 --> 01:34:17.183
I'll try, Daddy.


01:34:18.152 --> 01:34:20.487
Yeah.


01:34:27.662 --> 01:34:28.895
Hey, kiddo,


01:34:30.297 --> 01:34:32.198
so you're the man of the house now.


01:34:32.200 --> 01:34:33.867
You take good care of him, okay?


01:34:33.869 --> 01:34:35.335
I will.


01:34:35.337 --> 01:34:37.170
You should post that video.


01:34:37.172 --> 01:34:39.205
Okay.
Post it for me.


01:34:39.207 --> 01:34:40.740
I will.


01:34:41.442 --> 01:34:42.709
I love you, Sweetheart.


01:34:42.711 --> 01:34:44.110
I love you, too.


01:34:44.112 --> 01:34:45.768
That's great, man. Appreciate it.


01:34:46.615 --> 01:34:50.984
That kid of mine's been throwing
me curveballs my whole life.


01:34:50.986 --> 01:34:54.554
But luckily, I play baseball.


01:34:56.457 --> 01:34:58.858
Take care of my little girl up there, okay?


01:34:58.860 --> 01:35:00.827
You know I will, Sir.


01:35:00.829 --> 01:35:02.696
All right.


01:35:19.246 --> 01:35:20.547
Are you ready?


01:35:20.549 --> 01:35:22.148
What do you think?


01:35:27.488 --> 01:35:29.189
- Dad, can I have her--
- Her room?


01:35:29.191 --> 01:35:30.924
No, the car.


01:35:30.926 --> 01:35:32.025
Yeah.


01:35:32.027 --> 01:35:33.426
Yeah!


01:35:33.428 --> 01:35:34.761
In about ten years.


01:35:34.763 --> 01:35:36.396
Oh, man, come on.

